/* book exam traps: Saying maximum power transfer gives maximum efficiency. At RL = Rth the equivalent circuit is only 50 % efficient, and the real network can be worse. | Using P = Vth²/RL. The load voltage is not Vth; at the peak it is Vth/2. | Choosing Rs = RL when the load is fixed and the source resistance is the variable. Then the best source resistance is the smallest one. | Finding Rth with a dependent source switched off. The best load then comes out wrong (4 Ω instead of 3 Ω in worked example 2). | Using RL = Rth for an AC source with reactance. The condition there is the conjugate match. */
